      <p class="_abstract">OpenShift Container Platform includes default OAuth clients for platform authentication. You can register additional OAuth clients to integrate third-party applications and configure token inactivity timeouts to enhance security.</p>
      <h2 id="oauth-default-clients_configuring-oauth-clients" class="group scroll-mt-20">Default OAuth clients<a href="#oauth-default-clients_configuring-oauth-clients" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">OpenShift Container Platform automatically creates OAuth clients for browser-based logins, CLI authentication, and challenge-based authentication when the API starts.</p>
      <p>The following OAuth clients are created:</p>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>OAuth client</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Usage</TableHead>
